      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-114444",
      ":question/problem": "During lunch at a company, $50%$ of people choose a meal with chicken, $30%$ of people choose pork, and $20%$ choose a meal without meat. A sample of $12$ people is randomly selected. Find the probability that $6$ of them choose chicken, $4$ choose pork, and $2$ choose a meal without meat. Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
